UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 610, when internal auditors provide direct assistance, the external auditor must direct them regarding the nature, timing, and extent of work, supervise them during performance, and review their work for adequacy. The external auditor must also evaluate threats to the internal auditors'' objectivity and apply safeguards.
Wrong (A): Internal auditors providing direct assistance cannot work independently; they must be supervised by the external auditor at all times.
Wrong (B): Internal auditors may assist with various procedures beyond inventory observation when providing direct assistance.
Wrong (C): Internal auditors have no signing authority on the audit report; only the engagement partner signs.$EXPL$
