-- Q4575: Tests of Controls [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
-- STEM: A staff auditor on the Wellspring Energy engagement asks the manager whether inquiry of client personnel alone can ever be sufficient to test the oper
-- CHOICES (word counts):
--   A ★ (12w) Never ?????? inquiry alone does not provide sufficient evidence of operating effectiveness
--   B   (8w) When the control is performed by senior management
--   C   (11w) When the auditor has tested the control in the prior year
--   D   (8w) When the control is a simple manual control
-- CURRENT EXPLANATION: Inquiry alone is not sufficient to test the operating effectiveness of controls. While inquiry provides useful information, it must be combined with o
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 330, inquiry alone is never sufficient to test the operating effectiveness of controls. While inquiry provides useful information about design and implementation, it must be combined with other procedures such as observation, inspection, or reperformance to provide sufficient evidence of consistent operating effectiveness.
Wrong (B): The seniority of the person performing the control does not change the requirement to corroborate inquiry with other procedures.
Wrong (C): Prior-year testing does not eliminate the need to combine inquiry with other procedures in the current year.
Wrong (D): The simplicity of a manual control does not make inquiry alone sufficient; all controls require corroborating procedures.$EXPL$
