-- Q4588: Analytical Procedures [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
-- STEM: When performing substantive analytical procedures, the auditor must develop an independent expectation of the recorded amount. Which of the following 
-- CHOICES (word counts):
--   A ★ (15w) The data should be from a source that is independent of the account being tested
--   B   (7w) The data should be prepared by management
--   C   (11w) The data should come only from the prior year financial statements
--   D   (10w) The data should be provided by the entity's internal auditors
-- CURRENT EXPLANATION: When developing an expectation for a substantive analytical procedure, the reliability of the data is critical. Data used should be from a source that
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 520, when developing an expectation for substantive analytical procedures, the data should come from a source independent of the account being tested. Data reliability is critical; using data prepared or controlled by those responsible for the recorded amount reduces the procedure''s effectiveness and persuasiveness.
Wrong (B): Management-prepared data without verification is less reliable because it lacks independence from the account being tested.
Wrong (C): Limiting data to prior-year financial statements restricts the auditor''s ability to develop a robust independent expectation.
Wrong (D): Internal auditor-prepared data may be useful but is not inherently independent of the entity''s processes.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4588;

