-- Q4646: Specific Areas and Transactions [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
-- STEM: Beacon Electronics has reported operating losses for three consecutive years and recently failed to meet a key debt covenant. The engagement team is e
-- CHOICES (word counts):
--   A   (10w) The entity reported record high revenues in the current year
--   B ★ (11w) Recurring operating losses, negative working capital, and inability to obtain financing
--   C   (9w) The entity recently completed a successful initial public offering
--   D   (10w) The entity hired a new CEO with extensive industry experience
-- CURRENT EXPLANATION: Indicators of going concern issues include recurring operating losses, negative working capital, default on loan agreements, inability to obtain addit
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 570, indicators of going concern issues include recurring operating losses, negative working capital, default on loan agreements, and inability to obtain additional financing. These conditions raise substantial doubt about the entity''s ability to continue as a going concern for a reasonable period of time.
Wrong (A): Record high revenues is a positive indicator, not a going concern risk factor.
Wrong (C): A successful IPO provides capital infusion and is a mitigating factor, not a going concern indicator.
Wrong (D): Hiring an experienced CEO may be a positive step but does not itself constitute a going concern indicator.$EXPL$
