-- Q4649: Specific Areas and Transactions [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
-- STEM: Eastbrook Corp. reports $12 million in Level 3 fair value investments measured using a discounted cash flow model with management-developed assumption
-- CHOICES (word counts):
--   A   (7w) Accept management's fair value measurements without testing
--   B ★ (16w) Evaluate the reasonableness of management's assumptions, methods, and data used to develop the fair 
--   C   (8w) Only test fair value estimates for investment securities
--   D   (12w) Require that all fair value measurements be performed by an independent specialist
-- CURRENT EXPLANATION: The auditor should evaluate the reasonableness of the significant assumptions used by management, assess whether the methods and models used are appro
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 540, the auditor should evaluate the reasonableness of management''s significant assumptions, assess whether the valuation methods and models are appropriate, and test the accuracy and completeness of the underlying data. For Level 3 fair value measurements, which rely heavily on unobservable inputs, this evaluation is especially critical.
Wrong (A): Accepting management''s fair value measurements without testing violates the auditor''s responsibility to obtain sufficient appropriate evidence.
Wrong (C): Fair value audit procedures apply to all assets and liabilities measured at fair value, not only investment securities.
Wrong (D): Standards do not require an independent specialist for every fair value measurement; the auditor may test management''s estimates directly.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4649;

-- Q4650: Specific Areas and Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
-- STEM: During the audit of Chandler Holdings, the engagement team discovers that the CEO''s brother-in-law owns a major supplier. The team expands procedures
