--   D ★ (12w) Confirming all accounts receivable balances as a primary related party identification procedure
-- CURRENT EXPLANATION: While accounts receivable confirmations may incidentally reveal related party information, they are not primarily a related party identification proce
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): While accounts receivable confirmations may incidentally reveal related party information, they are not primarily a related party identification procedure. Under AU-C 550, standard related party identification procedures include inquiry, reviewing entity records, and examining public filings — not confirmation of receivable balances.
Wrong (A): Inquiring of management about the identity of related parties is a primary related party identification procedure per AU-C 550.
Wrong (B): Reviewing board meeting minutes for references to related party transactions is a standard identification procedure.
