-- Q4652: Specific Areas and Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
-- STEM: Collins & Price LLP was recently engaged to perform the first audit of Brightstar Logistics, which was previously unaudited. When auditing opening bal
-- CHOICES (word counts):
--   A   (11w) Accept the prior year's audited financial statements without performing any procedures
--   B ★ (19w) Obtain sufficient appropriate evidence that opening balances do not contain misstatements that mater
--   C   (12w) Only test opening balances if the prior auditor issued a modified opinion
--   D   (10w) Ignore opening balances because they relate to the prior period
-- CURRENT EXPLANATION: In an initial audit, the auditor must obtain sufficient appropriate evidence about whether the opening balances contain misstatements that could mater
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 510, in an initial audit the auditor must obtain sufficient appropriate evidence about whether opening balances contain misstatements that could materially affect the current period financial statements. This may include reviewing predecessor auditor workpapers, evaluating prior-year procedures, and performing specific procedures on opening balances.
Wrong (A): This entity was previously unaudited, so there are no prior audited financial statements to accept; even if there were, the auditor cannot accept them without procedures.
Wrong (C): Opening balance procedures are required regardless of whether a prior auditor issued a modified opinion.
Wrong (D): Opening balances directly affect the current period through beginning retained earnings and comparative amounts; they cannot be ignored.$EXPL$
