--   D   (10w) Issue a separate report on the prior year financial statements
-- CURRENT EXPLANATION: When comparative information is presented, the auditor should obtain sufficient appropriate evidence that the comparative amounts are free of material
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 710, when comparative financial statements are presented, the auditor must obtain sufficient appropriate evidence that prior-period amounts are properly stated and consistently presented. For continuing engagements, this typically involves reviewing prior-year workpapers and ensuring consistent application of accounting principles.
Wrong (B): A complete re-audit of the prior year is not required; the auditor performs procedures appropriate to the comparative information presented.
Wrong (C): Simply reading prior-year amounts without performing any procedures is insufficient to satisfy the auditor''s responsibilities.
Wrong (D): A separate report on the prior year is not required when the same auditor reports on comparative financial statements.$EXPL$
