-- CHOICES (word counts):
--   A ★ (6w) The financial statements as a whole
--   B   (9w) Only the specific accounts or assertions that are misstated
--   C   (5w) Only the entity's internal controls
--   D   (7w) The auditor's inability to complete the audit
-- CURRENT EXPLANATION: An adverse opinion relates to the financial statements as a whole. Even though the misstatement may originate in specific accounts, the adverse opinio
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 705, an adverse opinion relates to the financial statements as a whole. Even though the misstatement may originate in specific accounts, the adverse opinion states that the financial statements taken as a whole do not present fairly in accordance with the applicable framework.
Wrong (B): The adverse opinion is not limited to specific accounts or assertions; it covers the complete set of financial statements.
Wrong (C): An adverse opinion on the financial statements is separate from any report on internal controls; it addresses the financial statement presentation.
Wrong (D): An adverse opinion is based on identified misstatements, not the auditor''s inability to complete the audit, which would be a scope limitation.$EXPL$
